Package: mapAI
Title: Positional Accuracy Improvement for Geospatial Vector and Raster Data
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Konstantinos",
           family = "Vantas",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "kon.vantas@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-6387-8791"))
Description: A statistically rigorous, computationally efficient framework for
    Positional Accuracy Improvement (PAI) and differential distortion analysis
    of geospatial vector and raster datasets. Implements conformal similarity
    (Helmert via Ordinary and Total Least Squares), general affine, Thin Plate
    Splines (TPS), bivariate Generalized Additive Models (GAM) with thin plate
    regression splines and adaptive basis dimensions, and an extensible plugin
    architecture for custom machine learning algorithms. Features integrated
    spatial cross-validation (random, spatial clustered, spatial block, spatial
    buffered block, probability, and stratified) to prevent spatial autocorrelation
    data leakage. Supports topology-preserving vector transformation across all
    standard simple feature geometries with automated repair, in-memory raster
    rectification via damped Picard-Mann iterative coordinate inversion, and
    differential deformation diagnostics including Tissot's indicatrices,
    Cauchy-Green metric tensor invariants, and signed Jacobian topological
    inversion screening.
